\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Willingness to pay (WTP) for vehicle attributes by vehicle segment and budget tier, relative to a conventional vehicle. Points are mean WTP (in thousands of dollars) and bars are 95\% simulation intervals. BEV values combine the powertrain and range coefficients at 100, 200, and 300 miles, with vehicle age, mileage, and operating cost held equal to the conventional vehicle; solid intervals are within the range shown to that segment in the choice experiment and dotted intervals are extrapolated beyond it. Age, mileage, and operating-cost values are for a one-year, 10,000-mile, and one-cent-per-mile reduction, respectively.}}{17}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:wtp_vehicle_attributes}{{2}{17}{Willingness to pay (WTP) for vehicle attributes by vehicle segment and budget tier, relative to a conventional vehicle. Points are mean WTP (in thousands of dollars) and bars are 95\% simulation intervals. BEV values combine the powertrain and range coefficients at 100, 200, and 300 miles, with vehicle age, mileage, and operating cost held equal to the conventional vehicle; solid intervals are within the range shown to that segment in the choice experiment and dotted intervals are extrapolated beyond it. Age, mileage, and operating-cost values are for a one-year, 10,000-mile, and one-cent-per-mile reduction, respectively}{figure.caption.7}{}}
