\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Simulated Net WTP versus observed price premium: BEV pairs. Bars decompose WTP (powertrain, driving range, and operating cost) for real BEVs relative to each vehicle's closest conventional counterpart, by vehicle segment and budget tier. The blue point and error bar show simulated Net WTP (mean, 95\% interval); the dashed line is the observed mean price premium (or discount) at approximately three years of age. Operating-cost contributions use EPA-based fuel-cost differentials at \$3.18 per gallon of gasoline and \$0.17 per kWh of electricity. No matched BEV pair met the sample-size threshold for the high-budget SUV segment.}}{20}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:waterfall_wtp_bev}{{3}{20}{Simulated Net WTP versus observed price premium: BEV pairs. Bars decompose WTP (powertrain, driving range, and operating cost) for real BEVs relative to each vehicle's closest conventional counterpart, by vehicle segment and budget tier. The blue point and error bar show simulated Net WTP (mean, 95\% interval); the dashed line is the observed mean price premium (or discount) at approximately three years of age. Operating-cost contributions use EPA-based fuel-cost differentials at \$3.18 per gallon of gasoline and \$0.17 per kWh of electricity. No matched BEV pair met the sample-size threshold for the high-budget SUV segment}{figure.caption.8}{}}
